title: "Circle packing n=26: tolerance audit and exact certificate"
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: 2026-08-09
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21864592
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fernández Morales"
    given-names: "Juan José"
    affiliation: "Göther Labs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/juan-fernandez-gotherlabs/circle-packing-tolerance-audit"
keywords:
  - circle packing
  - exact certificate
  - numerical tolerance
  - computational geometry
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible artifacts for three numerical contracts of the n=26
  variable-radius circle-packing problem, including an exact-rational
  finite-decimal certificate, hash-authenticated public-corpus acquisition,
  tolerance-separated exact-rational reevaluation, contact-graph
  reconstruction, and a rational interval proof of strict local optimality
  for the enclosed 78-contact real root. No global optimum or universal
  packing record is claimed.
